From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: serialise the notification enable request

qcom_battmgr_request() reinitialises the shared ack completion and error
field, so its callers hold battmgr->lock; qcom_battmgr_enable_worker() did
not. After a PDR "up" it can run alongside a property request (0082
schedules the charge-policy worker at the same time), and either request
can then be completed by the other's answer: the policy acts on a stale
capacity, or a reply is lost and the request times out.

Take battmgr->lock around the request. Inherited upstream (linux-next
2026-10-02 is unchanged). Found by the 2026-10-02 GPT-6.1-Sol audit.

Hardware: restart the ADSP (or pmic_glink PDR) with a charge limit set;
battery properties and the charge policy must keep working.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 58a80bfd2..e0901e59a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -2386,7 +2386,10 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_enable_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 	};
 	int ret;
 
+	/* ack and error are shared with the property requests */
+	mutex_lock(&battmgr->lock);
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request(battmgr, &req, sizeof(req));
+	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(battmgr->dev, "failed to request power notifications\n");
 }
